# npm configuration for lifegame.
#
# This file deliberately declares no settings.
#
# Why there is no path here: npm resolves a relative path against the current
# working directory, and an absolute path would name one specific checkout — so
# either form breaks a clone or a git worktree of this repository by writing
# caches back into the original checkout. The npm cache is owned by
# scripts/env.ps1, which exports npm_config_cache computed from that script's
# own location and is mandatory before any toolchain command (AGENTS.md §1).
#
# Why there are no other settings here: the package manager for this project is
# pnpm, and pnpm 10 moved its settings to pnpm-workspace.yaml. The pnpm-only
# keys that used to live here made npm 11 warn about unknown configuration on
# every invocation, so they are gone; the defaults they were overriding are
# pnpm's own defaults.
#
# Authority: docs/plan/phase-01-foundation/acceptance.md — criteria A2, A10.
